<body>
    <div class="container">
        <header class="mt-5">
            <h1 class="display-4">Custom Macropad</h1>
            <p class="lead">A custom PCB-based macropad built for the Hack Club Blueprint program.</p>
        </header>

        <section>
            <h2>Project Description</h2>
            <p>This project involved designing and building a custom macropad that allows users to program specific keys for various functions. It was created as part of the Hack Club Blueprint program, which encourages students to engage in hands-on electronics projects.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Technologies Used</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>PCB Design Software (e.g., KiCad)</li>
                <li>Microcontroller (e.g., ATmega32U4)</li>
                <li>3D Printing for the case</li>
                <li>Programming in C/C++ for firmware</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Project Highlights</h2>
            <p>The macropad features customizable RGB lighting, programmable keys, and a compact design that fits comfortably on any desk. It was a great learning experience in both hardware and software development.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Images</h2>
